WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.556 --> 00:00:01.701
(Monika laughs)

00:00:01.701 --> 00:00:02.650
- [Mark] You're very fun to look at.

00:00:02.650 --> 00:00:05.431
- (laughs) Thank you.

00:00:05.431 --> 00:00:07.660
- [Mark] And we go again.

00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:08.493
- [Monika] So I'll just say everything

00:00:08.493 --> 00:00:11.693
and you could cut out
anything that you don't want.

00:00:12.730 --> 00:00:14.700
I'll just be as authentic.

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:15.533
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:00:16.650 --> 00:00:18.170
I just think it would
be good to have a talk

00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:21.760
about helping people, because
it's not as simple as like

00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:23.720
I think a lot of people see my videos and

00:00:25.244 --> 00:00:26.180
they see Caroline who we just spoke to,

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:27.480
or we see...

00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:30.377
Oh, it's an endless list of
people that come in here.

00:00:30.377 --> 00:00:32.457
"Oh my God, they just need
this, that and the other...

00:00:32.457 --> 00:00:34.090
"Don't you help them?"

00:00:34.090 --> 00:00:35.040
And I'm sure

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:38.350
we could probably shed a little light on

00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:40.280
what helping these
people is actually like.

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:41.113
- Sure.

00:00:41.113 --> 00:00:41.946
- [Mark] 'Cause that's what you do, right?

00:00:41.946 --> 00:00:43.251
- Yeah.

00:00:43.251 --> 00:00:45.700
So, I mean, since the first video,

00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:49.363
you and I have tried to
help a number of people.

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:53.750
I always try to basically
have interface with someone.

00:00:53.750 --> 00:00:55.577
So if Mark or anyone else says to me,

00:00:55.577 --> 00:00:57.650
"I have someone who really needs support."

00:00:57.650 --> 00:00:58.910
I want to sit down with them

00:00:58.910 --> 00:01:00.530
and I want to hear from them directly.

00:01:00.530 --> 00:01:03.300
I prefer if they're not high,

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:05.880
but I understand sometimes

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:07.150
that's unavoidable,

00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:08.950
especially when it comes
to things like crack

00:01:08.950 --> 00:01:10.720
'cause then it's really challenging.

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:13.789
Because crack does so much to your psyche.

00:01:13.789 --> 00:01:14.940
- [Mark] Crack is harder
to deal with heroin or--

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:16.140
- In my experience.

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:18.250
I'm not a doctor, but in my experience

00:01:18.250 --> 00:01:19.890
because of like this...

00:01:19.890 --> 00:01:21.770
Psychosis may not be the correct term,

00:01:21.770 --> 00:01:23.530
but because of what happens to someone

00:01:23.530 --> 00:01:24.610
when they're high on crack,

00:01:24.610 --> 00:01:26.900
the visions, the voices,

00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:30.200
it's really challenging to even
get to the core of a person

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:31.580
- [Mark] I mean, they're
all terrible drugs.

00:01:31.580 --> 00:01:32.413
And they're all...

00:01:32.413 --> 00:01:33.310
- They're all awful.

00:01:33.310 --> 00:01:34.830
But in terms of interfacing

00:01:34.830 --> 00:01:36.980
to find out if someone
is ready for treatment

00:01:36.980 --> 00:01:38.210
and if they really want this,

00:01:38.210 --> 00:01:40.800
it's more challenging with meth and crack

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:43.020
than it is some of the other drugs.

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:45.290
For me anyway, maybe that's...

00:01:45.290 --> 00:01:46.720
I don't know why would that would be

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:47.830
but that's how it's been

00:01:47.830 --> 00:01:49.790
because I can't get to a person.

00:01:49.790 --> 00:01:52.390
So, since the first video

00:01:52.390 --> 00:01:54.400
you've brought a number of people to me.

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:57.700
If they show up for the
meeting, like we just had one

00:01:57.700 --> 00:01:59.650
and they left in the middle of it

00:01:59.650 --> 00:02:00.770
because they were

00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:03.750
hallucinating or...

00:02:03.750 --> 00:02:04.583
- [Mark] What did she say?

00:02:04.583 --> 00:02:05.650
"No, I think I'm good."

00:02:05.650 --> 00:02:07.176
And then she just--

00:02:07.176 --> 00:02:08.040
- Yeah, we were in the
middle of talking about

00:02:08.040 --> 00:02:09.090
what treatment looks like

00:02:09.090 --> 00:02:11.680
and what her dreams
would be moving forward.

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:14.563
And she just said, "I'm good" and left.

00:02:15.678 --> 00:02:17.938
- No, and just to add,

00:02:17.938 --> 00:02:19.933
there have been more than a couple people

00:02:19.933 --> 00:02:22.460
that I've tried to help in a serious way.

00:02:22.460 --> 00:02:25.350
Like, cause what you're
offering is basically housing,

00:02:25.350 --> 00:02:28.810
an education, job
training, therapy, rehab,

00:02:28.810 --> 00:02:30.660
the whole thing on a silver platter,

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:32.800
all you gotta do is show up.

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:34.270
And we've had a couple people there,

00:02:34.270 --> 00:02:36.517
a couple of teenage people
that everyone was screaming at.

00:02:36.517 --> 00:02:39.070
"Oh my God, why don't
you help these people?"

00:02:39.070 --> 00:02:41.240
So we lined it all up with you,

00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:43.000
with your organization Patrick Cady.

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:43.833
And

00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:46.900
I don't want to name names

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:47.940
but if you've watched my channel

00:02:47.940 --> 00:02:50.160
you'll figure out who I'm talking about.

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:52.880
So we arranged an appointment
for that person to show up

00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:54.494
with you and me and

00:02:54.494 --> 00:02:56.370
we're gonna lay it all out for

00:02:56.370 --> 00:02:58.423
how we're gonna save your life.

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:00.533
We don't say it that way.

00:03:00.533 --> 00:03:01.847
We just like, "Would you like rehab?

00:03:01.847 --> 00:03:02.680
"Would you like housing?

00:03:02.680 --> 00:03:03.557
"Would you like an education?

00:03:03.557 --> 00:03:04.517
"Would you like some job training?

00:03:04.517 --> 00:03:06.170
"Would you like some therapy?"

00:03:06.170 --> 00:03:07.770
They say "Yes"

00:03:07.770 --> 00:03:10.710
and they fail to show
up for the appointment.

00:03:10.710 --> 00:03:11.820
And then we give them a second chance.

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:13.960
- Yes. Always.

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:15.870
- [Mark] And again, they fail to show up.

00:03:15.870 --> 00:03:18.043
So ultimately it becomes more about,

00:03:20.410 --> 00:03:21.823
getting them to accept,

00:03:23.710 --> 00:03:25.650
being fulfilled and happy in life,

00:03:25.650 --> 00:03:27.240
which is the biggest hurdle.

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:28.230
- It's really challenging

00:03:28.230 --> 00:03:30.440
and I don't fault the
people that don't show up

00:03:30.440 --> 00:03:33.620
and I don't have any
frustration toward them.

00:03:33.620 --> 00:03:35.400
I just think it's
important to give context.

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:36.360
And that context is,

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:39.200
these people have gone their
entire lives most of them,

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:41.840
being abused and being
told that they are nothing.

00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:44.640
So even if they are
presented with an opportunity

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:45.700
that you want to give them

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:47.610
or that Patrick Cady wants to give them,

00:03:47.610 --> 00:03:50.022
or is it Aurora?

00:03:50.022 --> 00:03:50.855
- [Mark] Aura.

00:03:50.855 --> 00:03:51.688
- Aura.

00:03:51.688 --> 00:03:52.650
Or that Aura wants to give them.

00:03:53.750 --> 00:03:56.810
It seems so unreal,

00:03:56.810 --> 00:04:00.640
that I think it just it's
like some sort of fantasy

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:02.630
alternate reality to where they are

00:04:02.630 --> 00:04:04.900
and they deserve the help but,

00:04:04.900 --> 00:04:07.580
the mental health aspect is what we don't

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:09.100
really have a grasp on.

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:11.540
And what brings someone to
the streets a lot of time

00:04:11.540 --> 00:04:13.610
and what brings someone to drugs is

00:04:13.610 --> 00:04:14.930
where they're at mentally

00:04:14.930 --> 00:04:18.180
and the abuse and the
mistreatment that's taken place.

00:04:18.180 --> 00:04:20.427
So it's like, you think,

00:04:20.427 --> 00:04:22.657
"Oh, well, here's this opportunity

00:04:22.657 --> 00:04:25.860
"that people would just
be running and lining up."

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:28.990
But that doesn't even align
with what brings someone

00:04:28.990 --> 00:04:31.173
to be in this place in the first place.

00:04:32.320 --> 00:04:35.540
If things were that easy,
they wouldn't be here.

00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:37.980
- [Mark] Yeah, as I said, I
think in the last Norman video.

00:04:37.980 --> 00:04:39.990
It's not about drugs.

00:04:39.990 --> 00:04:40.823
Drugs are not the issue.

00:04:40.823 --> 00:04:44.730
Drugs are just a symptom
of the much, much deeper

00:04:44.730 --> 00:04:46.403
and more stubborn problem of,

00:04:47.680 --> 00:04:51.010
loving yourself and being
able to accept a better

00:04:51.010 --> 00:04:52.280
life for yourself.

00:04:52.280 --> 00:04:53.510
Which they can't.

00:04:54.427 --> 00:04:56.000
And how do you fix somebody's childhood?

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:57.120
I don't even know.

00:04:57.120 --> 00:05:00.210
- It's like even the people
that I do get through to

00:05:00.210 --> 00:05:01.403
that we do work with,

00:05:02.350 --> 00:05:04.800
even after they've been
sober for a year or two,

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:06.690
it doesn't go away.

00:05:06.690 --> 00:05:08.180
And if anything, it gets louder.

00:05:08.180 --> 00:05:10.080
So kind of like I talked about before,

00:05:11.290 --> 00:05:14.500
it's such a large hurdle

00:05:14.500 --> 00:05:17.220
and it's so unbelievable to most people

00:05:17.220 --> 00:05:19.630
that someone would come in out of nowhere

00:05:19.630 --> 00:05:23.890
and make us a real effort to just,

00:05:23.890 --> 00:05:25.420
give them more opportunity

00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:28.240
when they've been taught
over and over for decades

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:31.050
that they don't deserve
those opportunities.

00:05:31.050 --> 00:05:35.460
So it's just, I mean, even
when we posted the last video

00:05:35.460 --> 00:05:36.810
I got a number of inquiries

00:05:36.810 --> 00:05:38.770
through Patrick Cady Foundation website.

00:05:38.770 --> 00:05:40.550
And I didn't get a single person

00:05:40.550 --> 00:05:41.800
that actually followed up with me.

00:05:41.800 --> 00:05:43.030
I emailed everybody back.

00:05:43.030 --> 00:05:45.417
I said, "Set a time to
have a call with me.

00:05:45.417 --> 00:05:46.907
"Let's discuss whether it be them

00:05:46.907 --> 00:05:48.240
"or their child or whatever."

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:51.300
I did have one mom that did respond to me,

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:53.840
that was saying, that explained
her daughter's situation.

00:05:53.840 --> 00:05:56.727
And I said, "Okay, I just
need your daughter to call me

00:05:56.727 --> 00:05:59.087
"because I'm not gonna get
somebody through treatment

00:05:59.087 --> 00:06:00.630
"if I can't talk to them first."

00:06:00.630 --> 00:06:02.680
There's no world where
I can even be of support

00:06:02.680 --> 00:06:04.960
or anyone else in our
foundation can do anything,

00:06:04.960 --> 00:06:06.450
if the person isn't willing
to have a conversation.

00:06:06.450 --> 00:06:08.310
Her daughter never called me.

00:06:08.310 --> 00:06:10.133
And it's not anyone's fault.

00:06:11.035 --> 00:06:14.280
But it's so deeply ingrained

00:06:14.280 --> 00:06:17.853
in people that end up in these situations.

00:06:20.063 --> 00:06:23.170
And again, it's such a large hurdle

00:06:24.473 --> 00:06:27.520
and we have to have such patience.

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:28.650
Like for what you do,

00:06:28.650 --> 00:06:30.883
I see you give money
to people all the time.

00:06:31.930 --> 00:06:35.880
It takes such patience to not
get frustrated or lose hope

00:06:35.880 --> 00:06:38.390
because all that we
want at the foundation,

00:06:38.390 --> 00:06:40.050
all that I want as a human being

00:06:40.050 --> 00:06:43.030
is to take care of other
people and help other people.

00:06:43.030 --> 00:06:45.550
And when nobody will show up and meet me

00:06:45.550 --> 00:06:47.260
or if they meet me and they walk out,

00:06:47.260 --> 00:06:48.680
it's like, "Oh, shit."

00:06:48.680 --> 00:06:50.473
Like how do I help?

00:06:51.610 --> 00:06:54.890
And I think that that's what
you're doing here is awareness.

00:06:54.890 --> 00:06:58.143
Awareness is how we help
because it's a concerted effort.

00:06:58.143 --> 00:07:00.530
- [Mark] I mean, I do more
than my share of helping.

00:07:00.530 --> 00:07:02.400
- You do, a lot (laughs).

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:04.090
- [Mark] And I try not to show that

00:07:04.090 --> 00:07:05.971
because I don't want this
to be a help channel.

00:07:05.971 --> 00:07:08.327
This channel I'm doing is not about,

00:07:08.327 --> 00:07:09.877
"Oh, let's help this person.

00:07:09.877 --> 00:07:10.710
"Let's help Caroline.

00:07:10.710 --> 00:07:14.530
"Let's help whoever,
you name your person."

00:07:14.530 --> 00:07:17.070
It's about creating awareness
so that we can prevent this

00:07:17.070 --> 00:07:18.970
'cause I see that as the real solution.

00:07:18.970 --> 00:07:20.590
'Cause I don't think we
can patch all these people.

00:07:20.590 --> 00:07:21.423
- No.

00:07:22.590 --> 00:07:23.960
- [Mark] There are
thousands of people here

00:07:23.960 --> 00:07:24.793
just on Skid Row.

00:07:24.793 --> 00:07:26.070
And there are other communities like this

00:07:26.070 --> 00:07:26.960
all across the country.

00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:29.950
And in every viewer's
hometown I guarantee you,

00:07:29.950 --> 00:07:31.650
there are people just like this.

00:07:31.650 --> 00:07:33.530
So you don't need to like
travel across the country

00:07:33.530 --> 00:07:35.023
and fix Caroline.

00:07:36.810 --> 00:07:38.360
If you want to help these people,

00:07:38.360 --> 00:07:40.890
figure out somebody right in
your backyard, that's doing it,

00:07:40.890 --> 00:07:42.740
doing the same damage to themselves.

00:07:42.740 --> 00:07:45.050
But the purpose of this channel

00:07:45.050 --> 00:07:47.540
is not about helping Caroline.

00:07:47.540 --> 00:07:50.370
The purpose of this
channel is to show you how,

00:07:50.370 --> 00:07:52.590
keeping families intact and together

00:07:52.590 --> 00:07:55.540
and supporting communities that are rich.

00:07:57.808 --> 00:08:00.310
Just churning over
generation after generation,

00:08:00.310 --> 00:08:03.940
after generation of these
uneducated, damaged people

00:08:03.940 --> 00:08:05.590
from broken families.

00:08:05.590 --> 00:08:07.070
That's gonna be the solution

00:08:07.070 --> 00:08:10.130
'cause I don't think we
can fix Caroline or...

00:08:10.130 --> 00:08:12.040
I mean, a lot of these
people that we're gonna...

00:08:12.040 --> 00:08:12.873
Let's say we did help.

00:08:12.873 --> 00:08:13.750
Let's say we got them rehab.

00:08:13.750 --> 00:08:15.110
We got them an education.

00:08:15.110 --> 00:08:16.170
We got them some job training.

00:08:16.170 --> 00:08:18.170
We got them some therapy.

00:08:18.170 --> 00:08:22.730
They still have a long,
long list of problems,

00:08:22.730 --> 00:08:25.440
like the inability to trust others.

00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:28.316
The inability to create trust from others.

00:08:28.316 --> 00:08:31.350
The inability to handle money.

00:08:31.350 --> 00:08:32.800
They see money, they burn it.

00:08:33.760 --> 00:08:35.281
It's what they do.

00:08:35.281 --> 00:08:36.114
They don't understand saving money.

00:08:36.114 --> 00:08:36.947
- They don't know any better,

00:08:36.947 --> 00:08:37.780
'cause they doesn't know.

00:08:37.780 --> 00:08:39.430
No one's taught them to save money.

00:08:39.430 --> 00:08:41.120
- [Mark] They don't understand
postponed gratification.

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:43.520
They don't understand
anything you need to do to

00:08:44.740 --> 00:08:48.373
fulfill your (mumbles), be
functional and have a happy life.

00:08:50.380 --> 00:08:51.900
That's why I think
prevention is the answer.

00:08:51.900 --> 00:08:53.230
And that's the purpose of this channel.

00:08:53.230 --> 00:08:56.560
It's not about fixing these
people 'cause I don't know,

00:08:56.560 --> 00:09:00.500
that you, me and 150,000 other people

00:09:00.500 --> 00:09:01.450
could actually help

00:09:02.480 --> 00:09:03.313
Caroline.

00:09:04.160 --> 00:09:05.710
Or who just walked out of here.

00:09:07.610 --> 00:09:09.290
It's such a big problem.

00:09:09.290 --> 00:09:13.520
And it's so difficult to help

00:09:13.520 --> 00:09:15.370
each and every one of these people.

00:09:15.370 --> 00:09:19.470
The purpose, again, I'm saying
it for the 400th time is

00:09:19.470 --> 00:09:21.190
let's see what's broken about our society

00:09:21.190 --> 00:09:22.390
so this doesn't happen.

00:09:22.390 --> 00:09:24.465
'Cause it's gonna happen again and again,

00:09:24.465 --> 00:09:25.650
and it's gonna grow and
it's already growing,

00:09:25.650 --> 00:09:26.600
look around your town.

00:09:26.600 --> 00:09:28.575
- Right. I know.

00:09:28.575 --> 00:09:32.130
Ever since COVID downtown in Skid Row is,

00:09:32.130 --> 00:09:33.930
just grown exponentially.

00:09:33.930 --> 00:09:35.030
- [Mark] Without even about COVID.

00:09:35.030 --> 00:09:36.700
COVID is a whole nother
problem that makes it worse.

00:09:36.700 --> 00:09:38.050
But--

00:09:38.050 --> 00:09:39.210
- But it's just growing and growing--

00:09:39.210 --> 00:09:41.220
- [Mark] This was growing rapidly
for the last 10, 20 years.

00:09:41.220 --> 00:09:43.090
And I'm sure it's gonna continue

00:09:43.090 --> 00:09:45.790
unless we do some things to
address what's causing it.

00:09:46.684 --> 00:09:50.480
- And for us as a nonprofit,
we do intend to help.

00:09:50.480 --> 00:09:52.910
But it's just important
that people understand

00:09:52.910 --> 00:09:55.540
what help really looks like
and who is actually willing

00:09:55.540 --> 00:09:57.260
to receive that help because

00:09:57.260 --> 00:10:00.110
it's proven to be
exceptionally challenging

00:10:00.110 --> 00:10:05.021
to find people that even want the help.

00:10:05.021 --> 00:10:05.854
- [Mark] That's right.

00:10:05.854 --> 00:10:06.687
That's it right there.

00:10:06.687 --> 00:10:07.520
Nobody really...

00:10:07.520 --> 00:10:08.700
They say they want it on video.

00:10:08.700 --> 00:10:11.080
I mean, there's been a
couple of people that

00:10:11.080 --> 00:10:13.297
sat where you're sitting and said,

00:10:13.297 --> 00:10:15.300
"I just wish somebody would help me."

00:10:15.300 --> 00:10:18.140
And your eyes start watering
and your heart opens up

00:10:19.460 --> 00:10:20.760
and you want to help them.

00:10:21.610 --> 00:10:24.010
And when the rubber hits the road

00:10:24.010 --> 00:10:25.650
they actually don't want the help.

00:10:25.650 --> 00:10:26.700
They can't accept it.

00:10:27.930 --> 00:10:28.763
And the answer is not to,

00:10:28.763 --> 00:10:31.650
"Oh, just well, screw them
and forget about them."

00:10:31.650 --> 00:10:34.120
Because I believe, I'm not religious

00:10:34.120 --> 00:10:35.720
but I believe you need to be like Jesus

00:10:35.720 --> 00:10:37.020
and just keep giving 'em a chance,

00:10:37.020 --> 00:10:37.853
keep giving 'em a chance,

00:10:37.853 --> 00:10:41.460
even when they screw up for the 15th time,

00:10:41.460 --> 00:10:43.459
you keep giving them a chance.

00:10:43.459 --> 00:10:44.928
- That's patience. We have to have that.

00:10:44.928 --> 00:10:45.761
- [Mark] That's what you need.

00:10:45.761 --> 00:10:46.610
And it requires so much.

00:10:46.610 --> 00:10:49.490
And I can't do it for all
of the 2000 people plus

00:10:49.490 --> 00:10:50.800
that I've interviewed.

00:10:50.800 --> 00:10:53.930
And there's 12,000 more
that I haven't interviewed.

00:10:53.930 --> 00:10:55.530
They're all surrounding me here.

00:10:56.990 --> 00:10:58.670
It's just too much for one person.

00:10:58.670 --> 00:11:00.320
And if you guys all want to fly out to LA

00:11:00.320 --> 00:11:02.100
and fix everybody on
Skid Row, come on out.

00:11:02.100 --> 00:11:03.970
But there's people in your hometown,

00:11:03.970 --> 00:11:07.740
in New Jersey or Philadelphia
or Miami or Chicago,

00:11:07.740 --> 00:11:09.870
wherever, that are in
the same exact situation.

00:11:09.870 --> 00:11:11.890
So you don't need to come here.

00:11:11.890 --> 00:11:15.460
This is not just an odd
situation that happens in LA.

00:11:15.460 --> 00:11:16.730
This is happening all across the country

00:11:16.730 --> 00:11:18.343
and probably all over the world.

00:11:19.450 --> 00:11:21.541
- Yeah. It really is.

00:11:21.541 --> 00:11:24.840
And it really just boils down to awareness

00:11:24.840 --> 00:11:27.130
and the willingness to be patient

00:11:27.130 --> 00:11:30.730
and the willingness to understand
the human condition enough

00:11:30.730 --> 00:11:33.480
to love these people outside of

00:11:33.480 --> 00:11:35.610
what you're seeing on
your YouTube channel.

00:11:35.610 --> 00:11:36.956
You know what I'm saying?

00:11:36.956 --> 00:11:38.240
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:11:38.240 --> 00:11:41.040
- Somebody taught them that
that's what they were worth.

00:11:41.040 --> 00:11:45.910
So again, it goes back to how
we're treating these children

00:11:45.910 --> 00:11:47.760
how we're keeping these families,

00:11:47.760 --> 00:11:49.280
what we're doing systemically

00:11:49.280 --> 00:11:51.820
to support people who need support.

00:11:51.820 --> 00:11:54.380
That's where we actually break this cycle.

00:11:54.380 --> 00:11:56.380
And as far as the people
who were already here

00:11:56.380 --> 00:11:58.720
we'll do everything we can.

00:11:58.720 --> 00:11:59.703
But it's hard.

00:12:01.220 --> 00:12:03.460
- [Mark] Yeah. I had
lunch with you a month ago

00:12:03.460 --> 00:12:05.080
and you said one of the
most interesting things

00:12:05.080 --> 00:12:06.620
I've ever heard,

00:12:06.620 --> 00:12:07.840
which I can't stop thinking about,

00:12:07.840 --> 00:12:08.673
which is,

00:12:11.810 --> 00:12:16.450
it's a recycling
multi-generational problem.

00:12:16.450 --> 00:12:19.215
Every family keeps doing
the same thing to their own

00:12:19.215 --> 00:12:20.270
and it just goes on and on.

00:12:20.270 --> 00:12:21.247
And I go, "When did this start?

00:12:21.247 --> 00:12:22.090
"Did it get worse?"

00:12:22.090 --> 00:12:23.397
And you said,

00:12:23.397 --> 00:12:25.410
"No, this is how the country was built."

00:12:25.410 --> 00:12:26.243
I'm paraphrasing.

00:12:26.243 --> 00:12:27.080
But you said something like,

00:12:27.080 --> 00:12:29.087
"This is how the United
States was created.

00:12:29.087 --> 00:12:30.577
"A bunch of Europeans came here,

00:12:30.577 --> 00:12:32.573
"raped and stole from the Indians.

00:12:33.577 --> 00:12:36.327
"And that generation did
it to the following gen...

00:12:36.327 --> 00:12:37.247
"It just continued on.

00:12:37.247 --> 00:12:38.767
"And it looks different

00:12:38.767 --> 00:12:39.677
"every a hundred years,
it looks different.

00:12:39.677 --> 00:12:42.007
"So now it's about homelessness and drugs

00:12:42.007 --> 00:12:43.277
"and all that kind of stuff.

00:12:43.277 --> 00:12:45.327
"But a hundred years ago, it
was, it looked very different

00:12:45.327 --> 00:12:46.970
"but it was all the same problem."

00:12:46.970 --> 00:12:48.650
- It was all the same problem

00:12:48.650 --> 00:12:50.330
and things were just more separate.

00:12:50.330 --> 00:12:53.111
- [Mark] Yeah, 'cause this
what the country was built on.

00:12:53.111 --> 00:12:54.470
- With the internet and everything else,

00:12:54.470 --> 00:12:57.050
we're getting exposed to
things that have been existing

00:12:57.050 --> 00:13:00.400
for the entirety of
this country's history.

00:13:00.400 --> 00:13:03.710
But before it was hidden
away in the projects

00:13:03.710 --> 00:13:06.250
or wherever it was and other people,

00:13:06.250 --> 00:13:08.700
people like us that are
privileged didn't see it.

00:13:08.700 --> 00:13:11.020
But it is we...

00:13:11.020 --> 00:13:12.770
This country started out

00:13:15.020 --> 00:13:16.853
with a violent intent.

00:13:18.073 --> 00:13:18.906
- [Mark] It was built on violence.

00:13:18.906 --> 00:13:20.510
- It was built on violence.

00:13:20.510 --> 00:13:23.060
So to unlearn that,

00:13:23.060 --> 00:13:23.990
we have to figure out

00:13:23.990 --> 00:13:25.970
how to have more of a sense of community.

00:13:25.970 --> 00:13:27.820
And that comes in at all angles,

00:13:27.820 --> 00:13:29.980
not everybody should be helping.

00:13:29.980 --> 00:13:31.790
Not everybody should be doing something.

00:13:31.790 --> 00:13:33.330
We just have to figure this out.

00:13:33.330 --> 00:13:35.320
And like you said, be like Jesus

00:13:35.320 --> 00:13:37.920
and have some patience and
understanding for people.

00:13:39.240 --> 00:13:40.536
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:13:40.536 --> 00:13:41.680
It's a huge problem.

00:13:41.680 --> 00:13:42.553
It's growing.

00:13:43.950 --> 00:13:45.960
And patching the broken
ones is not the answer.

00:13:45.960 --> 00:13:47.930
That's a simplistic attitude.

00:13:47.930 --> 00:13:49.560
I think you have to think much bigger,

00:13:49.560 --> 00:13:50.590
which is the purpose of my channel,

00:13:50.590 --> 00:13:53.563
is let's look at what's
wrong, what's broken,

00:13:54.460 --> 00:13:56.490
so that we can start
figuring out how to solve it.

00:13:56.490 --> 00:13:58.620
'Cause I don't even know if,

00:13:58.620 --> 00:14:00.870
doing things to keep families
together would it even work

00:14:00.870 --> 00:14:02.360
or be the total solution

00:14:02.360 --> 00:14:03.990
'cause then there's still the lack of hope

00:14:03.990 --> 00:14:04.823
in these communities.

00:14:04.823 --> 00:14:05.656
The lack of

00:14:06.910 --> 00:14:07.743
like...

00:14:09.186 --> 00:14:12.710
- It runs so deep and it's
so complicated and systemic

00:14:12.710 --> 00:14:14.540
that it seems

00:14:15.390 --> 00:14:17.930
impossible at times.

00:14:17.930 --> 00:14:22.860
But if we all start to have
the same conversations,

00:14:22.860 --> 00:14:24.933
it becomes more and more possible.

00:14:26.520 --> 00:14:27.353
- [Mark] Exactly.

00:14:27.353 --> 00:14:28.520
I think

00:14:28.520 --> 00:14:29.630
you can say it's about the family.

00:14:29.630 --> 00:14:31.510
You can say it's about
the lack of education

00:14:31.510 --> 00:14:33.830
or the lack of opportunities in

00:14:33.830 --> 00:14:36.150
some of the communities
that these people grow in,

00:14:36.150 --> 00:14:36.983
grow up into.

00:14:36.983 --> 00:14:37.816
But

00:14:39.210 --> 00:14:42.870
ultimately I hate to
be one of these people

00:14:42.870 --> 00:14:45.170
but it's ultimately about love.

00:14:45.170 --> 00:14:46.003
- Yeah.

00:14:47.170 --> 00:14:48.790
- [Mark] And if (mumbles)

00:14:48.790 --> 00:14:50.050
ever wants their name back,

00:14:50.050 --> 00:14:51.540
I would change the name
to Unconditional Love.

00:14:51.540 --> 00:14:54.237
Cause that's really what it's all about.

00:14:54.237 --> 00:14:55.390
- That's what we're missing.

00:14:55.390 --> 00:14:57.980
We're divided by politics
or divided by race.

00:14:57.980 --> 00:15:00.203
We're divided by all these things that,

00:15:01.420 --> 00:15:03.280
aren't doing us any good.

00:15:03.280 --> 00:15:07.320
We have to learn how to fall
back in love with ourselves

00:15:07.320 --> 00:15:09.540
and with each other and with the community

00:15:09.540 --> 00:15:10.373
that we're a part of

00:15:10.373 --> 00:15:12.520
because we have to take
care of this world,

00:15:12.520 --> 00:15:13.490
we only get one

00:15:14.610 --> 00:15:15.443
and that's it.

00:15:16.370 --> 00:15:18.500
So you and I will keep doing our part

00:15:18.500 --> 00:15:21.880
and everybody can do something
no matter how small it is

00:15:21.880 --> 00:15:25.090
buy the person behind you
when you're at Walmart,

00:15:25.090 --> 00:15:26.450
buy their stuff.

00:15:26.450 --> 00:15:27.520
If it's a mom with three kids

00:15:27.520 --> 00:15:29.170
and you can tell she's
struggling and you're okay

00:15:29.170 --> 00:15:33.760
just buy it, just do something
to give other people help.

00:15:33.760 --> 00:15:35.360
- [Mark] Beautifully said.

00:15:35.360 --> 00:15:36.707
Monika, you're amazing.

00:15:36.707 --> 00:15:38.440
- Thank you (laughs).

00:15:38.440 --> 00:15:39.273
- [Mark] Thank you so much.

00:15:39.273 --> 00:15:40.536
- Thank you.

00:15:40.536 --> 00:15:42.135
- [Mark] This was just an impromptu thing.

00:15:42.135 --> 00:15:43.630
We were trying to meet Caroline

00:15:43.630 --> 00:15:45.460
to help her get on in
one of your programs,

00:15:45.460 --> 00:15:47.990
and she turned on her heels and ran away.

00:15:47.990 --> 00:15:48.860
- And it's okay.

00:15:48.860 --> 00:15:50.500
Because if she decides she wants it again,

00:15:50.500 --> 00:15:51.340
I'll meet with her again.

00:15:51.340 --> 00:15:52.430
- Yeah, no, I love Carolina.

00:15:52.430 --> 00:15:53.263
She's the greatest.

00:15:53.263 --> 00:15:55.030
She's my original, like,

00:15:55.030 --> 00:15:57.380
the first friend I
really made down here and

00:15:57.380 --> 00:16:00.010
I've known her for 10 or 11 years and

00:16:00.010 --> 00:16:01.026
it hurts.

00:16:01.026 --> 00:16:01.859
It breaks my heart every
time I see her out there

00:16:01.859 --> 00:16:03.910
trying to pick up some
guy who's just gonna...

00:16:03.910 --> 00:16:04.790
- [Monika] Yeah.

00:16:04.790 --> 00:16:05.623
That's hard.

00:16:05.623 --> 00:16:08.640
- [Mark] Give her 30
bucks for some crazy act

00:16:08.640 --> 00:16:09.940
that she's gonna do and--

00:16:09.940 --> 00:16:11.076
- [Monika] I know.

00:16:11.076 --> 00:16:13.180
- [Mark] And it's just so sad that

00:16:13.180 --> 00:16:14.496
you're doing your part--

00:16:14.496 --> 00:16:15.329
- [Monika] We're gonna keep going.

00:16:15.329 --> 00:16:16.162
- [Mark] Yeah, you're amazing.

00:16:16.162 --> 00:16:16.995
Thank you so much.

